    "score": 5.570997642556349,
    "snippet": "---\ntitle: 15 Celebrity Dads Who Had Children After 50\nauthor: Sari Hitchins Updated\ndate: 2023-06-13\n---\nThere may be no perfect age to become a parent (did any of us really feel ready?), but the National Center for Family and Marriage Research reports the average age a man becomes a dad is between 27 and 30.\n\nFor some, though\u2014including these celebrities\u2014becoming a dad can happen at any age. In fact, some famous fathers have doubled the average, becoming dads past the age of 65. We have to hand it to them\u2014keeping up with an energetic toddler is hard enough in your 30s. We can't imagine it after retirement!\n\nHere are some older pops who had children later in life. Note: the ages listed below are the ages at which each celebrity had their latest child.\n\nAl Pacino, 83\n\nHollywood legend Al Pacino was expecting a baby with his 29-year-old girlfriend Noor Alfallah in the summer of 2023. Pacino already has three other grown children. He shares his oldest daughter, 33-year-old Julie Marie with ex-girlfriend Jan Tarrant. Pacino is also a father to 22-year-old twins Anton and Olivia with Beverly D'Angelo.\n\nRobert De Niro, 79\n\nIn May 2023, Robert De Niro announced the birth of his seventh child. He shares Gia Virginia Chen De Niro, with his girlfriend Tiffany Chen. Talk about an age difference\u2014there is a 51-year gap between De Niro's oldest child and his youngest child.\n\nDe Niro shares children Drena, 51, and Raphael, 46, with first wife Diahnne Abbott, has twin sons Aaron and Julian, 27, with his ex-girlfriend Toukie Smith, and has Elliot, 25, and Helen, 11, with ex-wife Grace Hightower.\n\nMick Jagger, 73\n\nPapa is a Rolling Stone! Mick Jagger welcomed his eighth child\u2014a son, with girlfriend Melanie Hamrick in 2016\u2014at the age of 73. According to The Daily Mail, the two have no plans of marrying, but the rock legend flew 3,500 miles from London to New York at the last minute to be with Hamrick for the birth.\n\nNow at age 79, Jagger has eight children in total\u2014sons James, 37; Gabriel, 25; and Lucas, 24"
