    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Don't forget the other brother! Here are the celebrity brothers you forgot came in threes (or more!)\nauthor: Mary Sollosi\ndate: 2025-01-29\n---\nFame can often run through a family, but sometimes it skips a sibling who works just as hard. While some duos like the Sprouse twins or Travis and Jason Kelce share equal time in the spotlight, there are famous brothers with lesser-known siblings quietly rounding out the family tree (Frankie Jonas missed his chance to join the Jonas Brothers because of his age; Cooper Manning's injury kept him off the field while his brothers made it big in the NFL; and the list goes on).\n\nIt's time to give these \"other brothers\" their due. Read on to meet the famous brothers you know \u2014 and their siblings who've flown under the radar.\n\nCharlie Sheen, Emilio Estevez, and Ramon Estevez\n\nSandwiched in between Emilio and Charlie in the Sheen-Estevez family tree is Ramon, another sibling who followed in the footsteps of their Emmy-winning father, Martin Sheen (also born Ramon Estevez), by stepping into the family business of acting. Ramon has worked alongside his family in several films like Cadence (1990) and Shadow Conspiracy (1997) and episodes of The West Wing and Grace and Frankie, but he's mostly stayed off screen since 2019. \u2014James Mercadante\n\nLiam, Chris, and Luke Hemsworth\n\nDon't forget about Luke Hemsworth just because he doesn't have an action franchise (though he did appear as Actor Thor in 2017's Thor: Ragnarok and 2022's Thor: Love and Thunder)! Chris and Liam's older brother is a successful actor as well, and starred on Westworld. \u2014Mary Sollosi\n\nLuke, Owen, and Andrew Wilson\n\nLuke and Owen Wilson's older brother, Andrew, is also an actor \u2014 he's appeared alongside his younger siblings in many of their films (including 2001's The Royal Tenenbaums, 2006's Idiocracy, and 2011's The Big Year), as well as a director (2005's The Wendell Baker Story; written, co-directed by, and starring Luke, with Owen in a supporting role). \u2014M.S.\n\nLiam, Noel, and Paul Gallagher\n\nNo, he wasn't in Oasis, but yes, there's another Gallagher! Liam and Noel's older brother, Paul"
