    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Screen Rant\nauthor: Jessica Baxter\ndate: 2018-02-14\n---\nThese days, marriage is a fragile institution. Hollywood stars know this better than anyone. But every once in a while, a famously separated couple will decide to give their love another go. Maybe they were too young the first time. Sometimes, one (or both) of them cheated or had a substance abuse problem. Maybe it just wasn't the right time.\n\nMultiple marriages are not at all uncommon in Hollywood. The stars on this list have all been married more than once - and at least two of those marriages were to the same person. For some, they realized their mistake after a short time apart and quickly reconciled. Some of those couples even managed to stay together for the long haul. For others, it was the second marriage that was the mistake.\n\nIn a couple of cases, these celebrities re-married more than one former spouse. A few of these stars have so many marriages on their resume that it practically became a hobby. It's quite possible that a few of these crazy kids will never quit each other. Who knows? They might even take the plunge a third time!\n\nHere are 20 Stars Who Married The Same Person Twice.\n\n20. Elon Musk and Talulah Riley\n\nSpaceX CEO Elon Musk met Westworld star Talulah Riley in 2008, and they married two years later. But their marriage only lasted as long as their courtship. In 2012, Musk tweeted to his soon-to-be ex, \"It was an amazing four years. I will love you forever. You will make someone very happy one day.\"\n\nMusk would be that someone when they reconciled 18 months later. Alas, they beat their marriage record by only 6 months. They filed for divorce on New Year's Eve 2014, but Musk soon withdrew the petition. A short while later, Riley filed in turn to file, and the divorce went through in 2016. Musk had a short-lived rebound with actress Amber Heard. He told Rolling Stone, \"If I'm not in love, if I'm not with a long-term companion, I cannot be happy.\"\n\n19. Eminem and Kim Mathers\n\nRapper Eminem (aka Marshall Mathers), wrote many songs about his longtime love, Kim. But since they weren't exactly Coldplay ballads, it's no surprise that their relationship had its ups and down. The childhood sweethearts met at a house party when he"
