    "snippet": "---\ntitle: The Top 50 Financial Technology CEOs of 2024\nauthor: Jirehl\ndate: 2025-06-09\n---\nThe Financial Technology report is pleased to announce The Top 50 Financial Technology CEOs of 2024. In an increasingly crowded fintech market, these leaders have managed to chart their own course. They have built companies that address key challenges in the financial services space, whether it's improving financial inclusion, simplifying insurance, providing real-time data for better decision-making, or streamlining complex procurement processes. These CEOs have not only responded to the industry's rapid evolution, but have led their companies in reshaping financial services.\n\nAmong this year's awardees, Doug Ricket, CEO and Founder of PayJoy, stands out for his pioneering work in providing access to credit in emerging markets, leveraging mobile security technology to make smartphones affordable through innovative financing solutions. Jackie Reses, CEO and Co-Founder of Lead Bank, stands out for her deep expertise in navigating complex banking regulations and her commitment to modernizing banking services through innovative technology, empowering builders and innovators to scale. Zachary Garippa, CEO and Co-Founder of Order.co, is known for his leadership in streamlining procurement processes, creating a platform that simplifies purchasing and payments for businesses while driving efficiency and cost reduction.\n\nThis year's awardees were selected through a methodical nomination process and careful consideration of each candidate's career track record and industry contributions. Please join us in celebrating The Top 50 Financial Technology CEOs of 2024.\n\n1. Simon Paris\n\nCompany: Finastra\n\nTitle: Outgoing CEO\n\nSimon Paris is the Chief Executive Officer of Finastra, a global provider of financial services software applications across lending, payments, treasury and capital markets, and universal (retail and digital) banking. The company's vision is to advance open finance through technology and collaboration, serving approximately 8,100 financial institutions, including many of the world's top banks. Paris is responsible for Finastra's strategic direction and growth, guiding the company in fostering industry collaboration and innovation within financial services.\n\nParis joined Finastra formerly Misys as President in 2015, was appointed Deputy Chief Executive Officer in 2017, and became Chief Executive Officer in June 2018. He brings more than 25 years of sales, management and global leadership expertise to the company, having previously held the role of President, Industry Cloud at SAP. Prior, he was a senior consultant with McKinsey & Company."
