    "score": 10.199575717925674,
    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Robotic Companion Pets\ndate: 2024-01-01\n---\nAt Capital Caring Health, one of the nation's oldest non-profit advanced illness and hospice providers, we strive to provide the highest-quality care for our patients. That is why we incorporate Robotic Companion Pets into our care plans for veterans, others with Dementia, and pediatric patients.\n\nSupport Our Robotic Pet Therapy Program\n\nWould you like to make a difference in someone's life? You can support our program and mission by making a one-time donation. The proceeds of every gift go right to work for Capital Caring Health services across the region. So, you can feel good that you are helping to make a difference in the comfort and care of patients and their families.\n\nPlease consider making a tax-deductible donation today. You can click a button below to support our Robotic Companion Pets Program based on how you'd like to give.\n\nThere are many known benefits to incorporating pet therapy into hospice and palliative care, including social isolation, loneliness, and cognitive decline. However, individuals withadvanced illnesses and their families may be unable to care for a live pet properly. That's where our robotic companion pets come into play.\n\nNumerous clinical studies have proven that these pets provide joy, comfort, and interactive companionship to patients and peace of mind to their families and caregivers. Veterans, other patients with dementia, and children often need extra care during this difficult time. In the hands of our patients, we almost always see immediate and positive responses, and their caregivers benefit as well.\n\nThe pets arrive ready to enjoy and interactively react to human touch and a voice like real pets. As we like to say, \"No need to feed or walk or clean up after them \u2013 just enjoy their love!\"\n\nCheryl-Lynne McCalla DO is a board-certified Family Medicine Physician. Dr McCalla is originally from Flossmoor, Illnois. She was an Air Force Flight Surgeon taking her from Virgina to Alaska and South Korea. Dr McCalla has worked as a Family Medicine Physician in Georgia and has recently relocated here to Virginia. Dr McCalla will be the Primary Care at Home team's Physician for Virginia patients outside the beltway.\n\nDr McCalla received her undergraduate degree in Biology from Tuskegee University and a Masters in BioMedical Science from Barry University prior to attending medical school at Lake Erie College of Osteopathic Medicine. She completed her Family Medicine Residency at Augusta University Medical Center.\n\n"
  },
