    "score": 7.970381452155644,
    "snippet": "---\ntitle: College of Business\ndate: 2020-03-19\n---\nCollege of Business\n\nDean's News and Insights\n\nRead prior messages from the Dean to students, faculty, staff, and friends of the College of Business, highlighting important news and key events.\n\nThe Dean's message is published in the monthly College of Business Newsletter. Visit the College of Business Publications page to find current and past issues of the newsletter and other publications on current happenings as well as stories on student success, community engagement, and faculty excellence.\n\nMay 2025 - COB Newsletter\n\nDear College of Business Community,\n\nAs we bring another remarkable academic year to a close, I find myself reflecting on the many moments that made this year unforgettable.\n\nLast week, we celebrated an important addition to our campus community with the opening of the new Asian Pacific Islander Desi American Center (APIDA Center). This vibrant space will serve as a source of support, connection, and pride for our students, furthering our commitment to inclusion and belonging here at CSUMB.\n\nWe proudly welcomed future students and their families to campus for two Admitted Otter Day events, one for Freshmen on April 12th, and one for transfer students on April 26th. Meeting our incoming students and seeing their excitement reminded me once again of the incredible energy and ambition each new class brings to our College. I look forward to seeing all that this next generation of Otters will accomplish.\n\nI am also delighted to share the news of our 2025 Dean's Medalist, Sarah Walter. Sarah exemplifies everything we hope for in our graduates: academic excellence, leadership, resilience, and a genuine dedication to serving others. We are incredibly proud of all she has achieved and excited to see the impact she will continue to make in the world.\n\nAnd finally, this year's College of Business Showcase was a night I will never forget. We came together to celebrate the achievements of our Capstone teams, recognize our outstanding students and leadership award recipients, and honor the donors, volunteers, and faculty who make our College so strong. One of the most meaningful moments for me was presenting Kukui bead necklaces\u2014a Hawaiian symbol of knowledge and enlightenment\u2014to our graduating seniors, marking the close of one chapter and the beginning of another.\n\nThis Showcase was especially personal for me, as it was my final one as Dean of the College of Business. I was deeply touched by the kind words and warm tribute shared that evening. Serving as your Dean has been one of the greatest honors of my career."
  },
